      dealing: 'Ante first. Each player receives two cards (one down, one up), dealt clockwise. After first betting round, one face-up card per active player, then betting; repeat until each has four face-up and one face-down (five cards total). Dealing pattern: clockwise.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Ante: Each player pays an agreed ante to the pot. 2. Initial deal: Each player receives two cards (one face down, one face up), dealt clockwise. 3. First betting round: Player with highest face-up card starts; ties broken by suit (hearts highest, then diamonds, clubs, spades). 4. Further deal and betting: Another face-up card is dealt to each active player, then a betting round (opener: best pair showing, or highest card, then second card; suits break ties). This repeats until each player has four face-up and one face-down card. 5. Showdown: After the final betting round, active players reveal hands; highest hand wins the pot.',
